<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Emile Griffith returns two weeks after intake with his care partner and is seen the same day by Dr. Haddad-Lindgren at the memory clinic. He had a brain MRI this morning. His intake blood count, metabolic panel, B12 and TSH were normal. He started sertraline 25 mg each morning after intake; he had mild nausea for three days, which has gone, and no dizziness or bleeding. The nightmares about the title fight still come most nights. His first session of cognitive processing therapy is booked for next week. He missed the physical therapy evaluation booked last week: the card was mislaid and nobody called to remind him. He has had no falls and has not travelled alone since intake. He has had no thoughts of suicide. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>MRI</td><td>Mild frontal-predominant atrophy; old right frontal injury; seven microbleeds; cavum septi pellucidi; hippocampi normal for age</td></tr><tr><td>CDR</td><td>Global 0.5, sum of boxes 2.0</td></tr><tr><td>Sodium</td><td>138 mmol/L two weeks into sertraline</td></tr><tr><td>Sertraline</td><td>25 mg; nausea for three days, now gone</td></tr><tr><td>Safety</td><td>No thoughts of suicide; safety plan on the refrigerator</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.18"/>
    <code code="10187-3" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Review of systems Narrative - Reported"/>
    <title>Review of Systems</title>
    <text><table><thead><tr><th>System</th><th>Result</th><th>Finding</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Neurological</td><td>Positive</td><td>Forgetfulness and slowness in finding words for names; no headaches, weakness, tremor or change in walking</td></tr><tr><td>Psychiatric</td><td>Positive</td><td>Nightmares most nights, guilt about the fight, mood low some days; no hallucinations, suspiciousness or thoughts of suicide</td></tr><tr><td>Gastrointestinal</td><td>Negative</td><td>Nausea in the first three days of sertraline, now gone; no diarrhea</td></tr><tr><td>Musculoskeletal</td><td>Negative</td><td>No falls</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>4 systems reviewed. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
</component>

